# The main document of the probe-query golden (SPEC §8.4, issue #68); its
# probe document is probe.ttl. `:p`'s two domains are disjoint, so `:p` can
# have no value, and `:q` can; A has an r-successor in B, and B is under C.
# The report is this document's alone: the probe lines follow it.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:p a owl:ObjectProperty . :q a owl:ObjectProperty . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:D a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class . :D owl:disjointWith :E .
:p rdfs:domain :D , :E .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :C .
